  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative launched on June 15th with Sarah Tan as the initial lead. The project has seen significant team expansion, including Mike Chen and Lisa Ray, and is exploring a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology. Key milestones include the completion of the testing phase (celebrated on October 10th) and a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two. The budget has evolved from an initial $500,000 for Phase One, to an adjusted $550,000, a compliance plan increase to $55,000, and a final executive approval of $2M covering all phases. A detailed report on Phase Two progress will be presented on November 20th."
